IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cra-types`
IMPORT `cra-goods`
IMPORT `cra-services`
IMPORT `cra-goal`

-- Independent tests: expected values decided from the Act and BRIEF.md
-- before the encoding was read (see independent-expectations.md).
-- A failing assertion is a finding; expected values are not to be edited.

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN tr IS A DATE, dl IS A DATE, ins IS A MAYBE DATE, per IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Goods supply`
mkG tr dl ins per MEANS `Goods supply` OF tr, dl, ins, per

GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Goods supply`
plain x MEANS mkG x x NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN rq IS A DATE, rc IS A DATE, bad IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Repair or replacement`
mkR rq rc bad MEANS JUST (`Repair or replacement` OF rq, rc, bad)

GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`, r IS A MAYBE `Repair or replacement`
GIVETH A DATE
stl g r MEANS `the last day for the short-term right to reject for` g `with` r

GIVEN fa IS A DATE, est IS A BOOLEAN, inc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Fault facts`
mkF fa est inc MEANS `Fault facts` OF fa, est, inc

GIVEN dl IS A DATE, fa IS A DATE, est IS A BOOLEAN, inc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
pres dl fa est inc MEANS `the goods are presumed not to have conformed on delivery for` (plain dl) `with` (mkF fa est inc)

GIVEN sa IS A BOOLEAN, sb IS A BOOLEAN, sc IS A BOOLEAN, mv IS A BOOLEAN, pr IS A NUMBER, ded IS A NUMBER, ex IS A DATE, ag IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tier two facts`
mkT sa sb sc mv pr ded ex ag MEANS `Tier two facts` OF sa, sb, sc, mv, pr, ded, ex, ag

GIVEN sa IS A BOOLEAN, sb IS A BOOLEAN, sc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
tier2 sa sb sc MEANS `the tier-two remedies are available under` (mkT sa sb sc FALSE 1000 200 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026))

GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`, mv IS A BOOLEAN, ded IS A NUMBER, ex IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
refund g mv ded ex MEANS `the refund on final rejection for` g `with` (mkT TRUE FALSE FALSE mv 1000 ded ex (Date 1 3 2026))

GIVEN nc IS A BOOLEAN, imp IS A BOOLEAN, fl IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Service facts`
mkS nc imp fl MEANS `Service facts` OF nc, imp, fl, JUST (Date 1 3 2026)

GIVEN nc IS A BOOLEAN, imp IS A BOOLEAN, fl IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
rp nc imp fl MEANS `repeat performance can be required for` (mkS nc imp fl)

GIVEN nc IS A BOOLEAN, imp IS A BOOLEAN, fl IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
prd nc imp fl MEANS `a price reduction is available for` (mkS nc imp fl)

GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
refby x MEANS `the last day for a refund agreed on` x

§ `A. s 22(3) — 30 days`

-- A1
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
-- A2
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS Date 4 4 2026
-- A3
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS Date 9 4 2026
-- A4
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) (JUST (Date 12 3 2026)) NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS Date 11 4 2026
-- A5
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 12 3 2026) (Date 12 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS Date 11 4 2026
-- A6
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 15 12 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- A7
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 2 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
-- A8
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 2 2028)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 2 3 2028
-- A9
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 31 1 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 2 3 2026

§ `B. s 22(4) — perishables`

-- B1 shorter period of 7 days ends 8 Mar
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 8 3 2026))) NOTHING EQUALS Date 8 3 2026
-- B2
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 2 3 2026))) NOTHING EQUALS Date 2 3 2026
-- B3
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
-- B4 "perishable" period longer than 30 days: not shorter
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 4 2026))) NOTHING EQUALS Date 31 3 2026

§ `C. s 22(6)-(8) — waiting period, 7-day rule`

-- C1
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 19 3 2026) FALSE) EQUALS Date 10 4 2026
-- C2
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 19 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 10 4 2026
-- C3
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 28 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) FALSE) EQUALS Date 3 4 2026
-- C4
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 28 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 6 4 2026
-- C5 request on the last day
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 7 4 2026
-- C6
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 27 4 2026
-- C7
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) FALSE) EQUALS Date 21 4 2026
-- C8 request after the limit: no revival
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 5 4 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
-- C9
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
-- C10
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 1 3 2026)) (mkR (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
-- C11 perishable (limit 8 Mar) with a 2-day waiting period
#ASSERT stl (mkG (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 8 3 2026))) (mkR (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 4 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 11 3 2026
-- C12 across the year end
#ASSERT stl (plain (Date 15 12 2025)) (mkR (Date 20 12 2025) (Date 3 1 2026) TRUE) EQUALS Date 29 1 2026

§ `D. s 19(14)-(15) — six-month presumption`

-- D1
#ASSERT pres (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 14 7 2026) FALSE FALSE
-- D2
#ASSERT NOT (pres (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 7 2026) FALSE FALSE)
-- D3
#ASSERT pres (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE FALSE
-- D4
#ASSERT pres (Date 31 8 2025) (Date 27 2 2026) FALSE FALSE
-- D5 [month-end]
#ASSERT pres (Date 31 8 2025) (Date 28 2 2026) FALSE FALSE
-- D6
#ASSERT NOT (pres (Date 31 8 2025) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE)
-- D7
#ASSERT pres (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 8 2026) FALSE FALSE
-- D8
#ASSERT NOT (pres (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) FALSE FALSE)
-- D9 [month-end, leap]
#ASSERT pres (Date 30 8 2027) (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE
-- D10
#ASSERT NOT (pres (Date 29 8 2027) (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE)
-- D11
#ASSERT pres (Date 29 8 2027) (Date 28 2 2028) FALSE FALSE
-- D12 s 19(15)(a)
#ASSERT NOT (pres (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE)
-- D13 s 19(15)(b)
#ASSERT NOT (pres (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE)
-- D14
#ASSERT pres (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE

§ `E. s 24(5)`

-- E1
#ASSERT tier2 TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- E2
#ASSERT tier2 FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- E3
#ASSERT tier2 FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- E4
#ASSERT NOT (tier2 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E5
#ASSERT tier2 TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `F. s 24(8)-(11) — refund and deduction for use`

-- F1
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 15 1 2026)) FALSE 200 (Date 15 7 2026) EQUALS 1000
-- F2
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 15 1 2026)) FALSE 200 (Date 16 7 2026) EQUALS 800
-- F3
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 15 1 2026)) TRUE 200 (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS 800
-- F4
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 15 1 2026)) TRUE 200 (Date 16 7 2026) EQUALS 800
-- F5 [month-end]
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 30 8 2025)) FALSE 200 (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS 1000
-- F6
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 30 8 2025)) FALSE 200 (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS 800
-- F7
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 31 1 2026)) FALSE 200 (Date 31 7 2026) EQUALS 1000
-- F8
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 31 1 2026)) FALSE 200 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS 800
-- F9 installation notice sets the start
#ASSERT refund (mkG (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 20 1 2026)) NOTHING) FALSE 200 (Date 10 7 2026) EQUALS 1000
-- F10
#ASSERT refund (mkG (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 20 1 2026)) NOTHING) FALSE 200 (Date 21 7 2026) EQUALS 800
-- F11
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 15 1 2026)) FALSE 0 (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS 1000
-- F12
#ASSERT refund (plain (Date 15 1 2026)) FALSE 200 (Date 16 1 2026) EQUALS 1000

§ `G. ss 20(15), 56(4) — 14 days`

-- G1
#ASSERT refby (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 14 3 2026
-- G2
#ASSERT refby (Date 20 12 2025) EQUALS Date 2 1 2026
-- G3
#ASSERT refby (Date 16 2 2026) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
-- G5
#ASSERT refby (Date 25 12 2027) EQUALS Date 7 1 2028

§ `H. ss 54-56 — services`

-- H1
#ASSERT rp TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (prd TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- H2
#ASSERT NOT (rp TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT prd TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- H3
#ASSERT rp TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT prd TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- H4
#ASSERT NOT (rp FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (prd FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- H5
#ASSERT NOT (rp FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (prd FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- H6
#ASSERT NOT (rp TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT prd TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Top-level goal (G4 and an end-to-end case)`

GIVEN g IS A MAYBE `Goods supply`, r IS A MAYBE `Repair or replacement`, f IS A MAYBE `Fault facts`, t IS A MAYBE `Tier two facts`, s IS A MAYBE `Service facts`
GIVETH A `Consumer position`
pos g r f t s MEANS `the consumer position for` (`Consumer case` OF g, r, f, t, s)

-- G4: services refund, agreed 1 Mar 2026
svc MEANS pos NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (mkS TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT svc's `last day for the service refund` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
#ASSERT svc's `service price reduction available` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT svc's `repeat performance can be required` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT svc's `last day for the short-term right to reject` EQUALS NOTHING

-- End-to-end goods: delivered 15 Jan 2026; repair 20 Jan-25 Jan, still faulty;
-- fault 1 Mar; final right exercised 1 Mar (first 6 months), not motor; agreed 2 Mar.
gds MEANS pos (JUST (plain (Date 15 1 2026))) (mkR (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 25 1 2026) TRUE) (JUST (mkF (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE)) (JUST (mkT TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 200 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026))) NOTHING
-- 14 Feb + 6 days = 20 Feb (7(b)); 7(a) = 1 Feb
#ASSERT gds's `last day for the short-term right to reject` EQUALS JUST (Date 20 2 2026)
#ASSERT gds's `presumed not to conform on delivery` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT gds's `tier-two remedies available` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT gds's `refund on final rejection` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT gds's `last day for the goods refund` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT gds's `repeat performance can be required` EQUALS NOTHING
